Suggests:
 openrgb (>= 1.0),
Description: Wild OS keyboard and mouse lighting
 Sets RGB keyboards, mice and other USB lighting to the colour and effect
 of the taskbar underglow, through OpenRGB, when Settings has it turned on.
 .
 OpenRGB's server runs only while the lighting is on and the session is in
 front, and listens on the loopback only. OpenRGB's own udev rules are
 replaced with narrower ones: the person at the screen gets the hidraw
 nodes of supported USB devices, except those that report key presses, and
 nothing else.
